NET current expenditure - NET REVENUE EXPENDITURE (TOTAL OF LINES 800 TO 804)","form":"RS","row":"805","col":"1"}}]}],"context":[{"label":"Resident population","value":87946,"year":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":2647000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":29139,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":32864,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2615.22,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":202.54,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":null,"compliance":null,"documents":[],"read_documents":[],"calendar":null,"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Exceptional Hardship Fund exhausted in 2025/26, indicating social pressure on vulnerable residents","lead":"An exhausted hardship fund signals significant social pressures and demand on the council that may indicate wider economic stress in the area affecting council finances. It could also indicate reputational or political risk around support for vulnerable\u2026","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Asset Management Strategy is aged and requires refresh in 2026","lead":"An outdated asset management strategy means the council's substantial property portfolio (\u00a386.65m) may not be optimally managed or aligned with corporate priorities. This could affect value realisation and borrowing capacity.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Debt management has notable weaknesses in aged debt recovery, system use and recovery consistency","lead":"Weak debt management directly impacts cash flow and income collection. Aged debt that is not being recovered reduces the council's cash position. The reliance on a single point of failure increases operational risk.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"South Hams Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","headline":"Exceptional Hardship Fund exhausted in 2025/26, indicating social pressure on vulnerable residents","detail":"The council's hardship fund for Council Tax Support recipients ran out of money during 2025/26 and will only reopen in April 2026. This suggests demand for support exceeded the budgeted provision.","category":"other","matters":"An exhausted hardship fund signals significant social pressures and demand on the council that may indicate wider economic stress in the area affecting council finances. It could also indicate reputational or political risk around support for vulnerable residents.","figures":"EHF exhausted in 2025/26; budget timing shows expected reopening April 2026","quote":"The SHDC EHF has been exhausted for 2025/26 and will re-open in April 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"South Hams Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","headline":"Asset Management Strategy is aged and requires refresh in 2026","detail":"The council's Asset Management Strategy is described as 'aged' and will be refreshed during 2026. Currently, the management of the \u00a386.65m property portfolio relies on officers' familiarity rather than being guided by an up-to-date strategy or asset management plan.","category":"audit","matters":"An outdated asset management strategy means the council's substantial property portfolio (\u00a386.65m) may not be optimally managed or aligned with corporate priorities. This could affect value realisation and borrowing capacity.","figures":"\u00a386.65m total property value (up from \u00a381.89m in 2023/24)","quote":"The aged Asset Management Strategy is to be refreshed during 2026. There is no Asset Management Plan to guide management of individual assets and to ensure alignment with corporate priorities.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"South Hams Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","headline":"Debt management has notable weaknesses in aged debt recovery, system use and recovery consistency","detail":"The audit identified weaknesses in aged debt recovery, system utilisation and consistency of recovery practice. Management is responding by proposing a dedicated debt recovery officer post, though this is still awaiting approval.","category":"audit","matters":"Weak debt management directly impacts cash flow and income collection. Aged debt that is not being recovered reduces the council's cash position. The reliance on a single point of failure increases operational risk.","figures":"Weaknesses identified in recovery practice and performance monitoring; proposal for new dedicated officer","quote":"There remains a sound underlying system of oversight and debt recovery procedures. However, notable weaknesses remain, particularly within aged debt recovery, system utilisation and consistency of recovery practice and performance monitoring.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"South Hams Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","headline":"Dartmouth Ferry service received Limited Assurance due to control weaknesses","detail":"One service audit received a Limited Assurance opinion, meaning significant gaps and weaknesses were identified. A new ferry income system is scheduled for June 2026 to address this, with follow-up audit planned.","category":"audit","matters":"Limited Assurance is a significant concern showing that control environment in a specific service is inadequate to effectively manage risks. This is the lowest assurance level received (excluding No Assurance).","figures":"1 audit out of 37 completed received Limited Assurance","quote":"There has been only one audit with a 'Limited' Assurance (This should be addressed by the introduction of the new ferry income System, scheduled for June 2026, that we will follow up on this year).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"South Hams Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Progress on the 2025-26 Internal Audit Plan and Annual Opinion","paper_url":"https://democracy.swdevon.gov.uk/documents/s36399/36399.pdf","headline":"Overall control opinion is Reasonable Assurance, not Substantial - meaning identified gaps could affect financial management","detail":"The Chief Internal Auditor's opinion is Reasonable rather than Substantial. This means some issues and non-compliance were identified that may put at risk the achievement of objectives. This is a lower level of assurance than the highest category.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender would need to understand that there are control gaps in the authority's financial governance. Reasonable Assurance indicates room for improvement in risk management and control.","figures":"One audit received Limited Assurance; multiple audits received only Reasonable Assurance","quote":"There is a generally sound system of governance, risk management and control in place. Some issues, non-compliance or scope for improvement were identified which may put at risk the achievement of objectives in the area audited.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-30"},"name":"South Hams","findings_total":103,"news_drafts_total":3}}